  "question": {
    "text": "The acceptor level of a p-type semiconductor is 6 eV . The maximum wavelength of light which can create a hole would be : Given hc $=1242 \\mathrm{eV}$ nm ."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "407 nm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "414 nm",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "207 nm",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "103.5 nm",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Energy is, $\\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda}$\n$\\mathrm{E}=\\frac{1242 \\mathrm{~nm}-\\mathrm{eV}}{\\lambda} \\Rightarrow \\lambda=\\frac{1242}{6}=207 \\mathrm{~nm}$"
  }
}